  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Latest sfc analysis shows deepening low pressure\nlifting towards SE VA this afternoon, and will continue to lift\nnorthward this evening. Band of showers and iso storms will \ncontinue to lift along the Outer Banks over the next hour or \ntwo, with conditions quickly drying late this afternoon and \nearly evening. Winds inc yet again tonight into Friday as strong\nCAA arrives with digging upper low, and with a well mixed lower\natms due to the CAA, winds will be quite gusty tonight into \nFriday, with gusts aoa 30 mph for inland areas, and 35-45 mph or\nso for the immediate coast and esp the OBX. Will hold off on \nWind Advisory for OBX but could be close at times. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...ENC is currently experiencing the next round of\nking tides this week with an increase in antecedant water \nlevels. Water levels have peaked for most of the area, with\nconditions gradually improving tonight into Friday. \n\nOceanside impacts will cont on the OBX into Friday, with large\nseas 10+ ft. As the aforementioned swrly winds inc tonight \nthrough Fri, the threat for OBX soundside flooding increases \nwith minor to moderate impacts possible with the latest increase\nin expected winds here. CF Warnings and Advisories continue for\nportions of the coast, along with High Surf Advisory (rough \nsurf and beach erosion).",
